WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:05.80
This is journey four of Hewn, the software factory: limit spending.

00:00:05.80 --> 00:00:09.08
Hewn runs without anyone approving each model call,

00:00:09.08 --> 00:00:13.44
so it has to know what every call costs, and stop itself at a limit.

00:00:13.44 --> 00:00:17.94
This video walks through how it was built: the meter, the price table,

00:00:17.94 --> 00:00:20.57
the budget rule, the page, and the tests.

00:00:21.72 --> 00:00:27.38
Every model call records its input and output tokens, its model and its cost,

00:00:27.38 --> 00:00:30.76
against its run, stage, direction and project.

00:00:30.76 --> 00:00:33.99
Spend shows on the project and updates live.

00:00:34.34 --> 00:00:36.21
Every direction has a budget.

00:00:36.21 --> 00:00:39.50
It starts at the default an Owner sets in Settings,

00:00:39.50 --> 00:00:41.76
and can be changed when submitting.

00:00:41.76 --> 00:00:45.89
At eighty percent, a warning is pushed and shown on the project.

00:00:45.89 --> 00:00:50.79
At one hundred percent, the direction pauses with the reason Budget reached,

00:00:50.79 --> 00:00:52.66
after the current model call.

00:00:52.66 --> 00:00:55.18
This is a safety stop, not an approval.

00:00:56.33 --> 00:01:00.96
Here is where usage is recorded, and how the threshold check runs.

00:01:00.96 --> 00:01:06.71
The worker reports each call the moment it returns, with its model and its tokens,

00:01:06.71 --> 00:01:07.91
but never a cost.

00:01:07.91 --> 00:01:11.41
The API prices the call, adds it to the direction,

00:01:11.41 --> 00:01:15.06
and answers with a verdict: continue, warn, or stop.

00:01:15.41 --> 00:01:19.26
In the worker, every call gets a fresh call identifier,

00:01:19.26 --> 00:01:21.49
so a retried report counts once.

00:01:21.49 --> 00:01:24.71
A warn verdict writes a line into the run log.

00:01:24.71 --> 00:01:29.88
A stop verdict ends the run straight away: no further call, no checkpoint,

00:01:29.88 --> 00:01:30.86
and no result.

00:01:32.01 --> 00:01:37.78
Prices are configuration: dollars per million input and output tokens for each model,

00:01:37.78 --> 00:01:40.70
defaulting to Anthropic's published prices.

00:01:40.70 --> 00:01:45.59
A model that is not in the table is priced at the table's highest rates,

00:01:45.59 --> 00:01:50.34
so an unknown model can only make the budget stop sooner, never later.

00:01:50.34 --> 00:01:53.19
Costs are kept to a millionth of a dollar.

00:01:54.34 --> 00:01:59.32
Recording the call and judging the budget happen in one handler, in one save.

00:01:59.32 --> 00:02:04.23
The first time spend reaches eighty percent, the direction is marked warned,

00:02:04.23 --> 00:02:06.94
and a budget warning event goes out, once.

00:02:06.94 --> 00:02:09.79
At one hundred percent, the verdict is stop.

00:02:10.14 --> 00:02:14.37
Stop pauses the run, its stage, the direction and the project,

00:02:14.37 --> 00:02:15.94
and releases the lease.

00:02:15.94 --> 00:02:21.60
The run keeps its checkpoint, so raising the budget in journey five can resume from

00:02:21.60 --> 00:02:23.24
the last completed step.

00:02:24.39 --> 00:02:28.30
The project header shows the direction's spend of its budget,

00:02:28.30 --> 00:02:30.62
as a meter with the amounts in text.

00:02:30.62 --> 00:02:33.19
Each spend updated event moves it, live.

00:02:33.19 --> 00:02:37.04
When the budget warning arrives, the meter turns to warning,

00:02:37.04 --> 00:02:40.57
and a toast says how close the direction is to pausing.

00:02:40.57 --> 00:02:43.40
The toast waits while you hover or focus it,

00:02:43.40 --> 00:02:46.87
and the meter keeps the news after the toast has gone.

00:02:47.22 --> 00:02:51.59
A paused direction shows Paused, Budget reached, with what it spent.

00:02:51.59 --> 00:02:56.22
And Settings has the default budget, which Owners save and Viewers read.

00:02:57.37 --> 00:03:01.27
The backend and worker slices began with their tests failing.

00:03:01.27 --> 00:03:04.71
The backend gained sixteen tests against the real API,

00:03:04.71 --> 00:03:07.20
and the worker four against a fake API.

00:03:07.20 --> 00:03:12.49
One backend test covers a race this journey uncovered: a log batch and a model call

00:03:12.49 --> 00:03:15.94
arriving at once, both claiming the same event number.

00:03:15.94 --> 00:03:18.11
Now a project's writes take turns.

00:03:18.11 --> 00:03:22.00
All green, the backend has one hundred and sixty three tests,

00:03:22.00 --> 00:03:24.42
and the worker one hundred and thirty.

00:03:24.77 --> 00:03:27.44
The frontend has forty five unit tests.

00:03:27.44 --> 00:03:32.91
End to end, a new pipeline test drives a real worker through the warning and the

00:03:32.91 --> 00:03:37.83
pause, and new behaviour, accessibility and visual tests cover Settings,

00:03:37.83 --> 00:03:40.50
for forty five end to end tests in all.

00:03:41.65 --> 00:03:42.75
Here is Settings.

00:03:42.75 --> 00:03:47.05
An Owner types a default of five dollars, and is told what to fix,

00:03:47.05 --> 00:03:48.68
with a link to the field.

00:03:48.68 --> 00:03:52.85
Three hundred and fifty saves, and new directions start with it.

00:03:53.20 --> 00:03:58.20
Now a direction with a ten dollar budget, and a worker that reports a model call

00:03:58.20 --> 00:03:59.20
every few lines.

00:03:59.20 --> 00:04:00.96
Each call costs sixty cents.

00:04:00.96 --> 00:04:04.21
Spend climbs in the header as each call is recorded,

00:04:04.21 --> 00:04:06.96
through the first stage and into the second.

00:04:06.96 --> 00:04:10.84
At eighty percent, the warning toast arrives, the meter turns,

00:04:10.84 --> 00:04:14.10
and the warning is written into the run log as well.

00:04:14.10 --> 00:04:19.35
A few calls later, the direction pauses, with Budget reached, and nothing more runs.

00:04:19.70 --> 00:04:22.83
The same page works in dark mode and on a phone.

00:04:22.83 --> 00:04:25.57
And a Viewer sees the defaults, read only.

00:04:26.72 --> 00:04:28.41
Journey four is complete.

00:04:28.41 --> 00:04:32.74
Every model call is recorded and priced by Hewn, not the worker.

00:04:32.74 --> 00:04:36.25
Spend climbs live, with a warning at eighty percent.

00:04:36.25 --> 00:04:41.52
And at one hundred percent, the direction stops itself after the current call.

00:04:41.52 --> 00:04:45.11
Next comes journey five: raise the budget and resume.
